[statement]
apk decides the request's names in the order it sorts them, ignoring ASCII
case (`requested-names-in-name-order-ignoring-case`): `x` before `Y`, so
`x` takes `p1`, and `Y` then `p2`. In byte order `Y` would come first, take
`p2`, and `p2` would answer `x` too.

[repository]
P:p1
V:1
p:x
k:100

P:p2
V:1
p:x Y=1
k:10

P:p3
V:1
p:Y=1

[request]
Y
x

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p1 1
install p2 1
